From a96a8b006be84e1a339aef2f9b7e6f17d598aca3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 18:14:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1101/1102] SableOS: Mobile Manager, App lock, Focus mode and
 profile model

Pure Java (no android.* imports) model for the Mobile Manager pages
(MOBILE_MANAGER_APP_CONTROLS_UX, PRIVATE_SPACE_DUAL_APPS_WORK_PROFILE_UX),
next to the Network Manager model it reuses:

* PackageSet: the stored package lists (App lock choices, Focus pause
  choices, what Focus actually paused); malformed names are dropped on
  read so a damaged value never names a package.
* AppLockPolicy: eligibility (launcher apps; never Settings, home,
  dialer, keyboard, system UI) and an honest status. LineageOS 23.2 has
  no launch gate, so PLATFORM_ENFORCEMENT is NOT_ENFORCED and a chosen
  app is never reported as locked.
* FocusModePolicy: the mode's notification policy (priority apps,
  alarms, media and repeat callers only), the per-app "can interrupt"
  state over Android's channel bypass store, pause eligibility, and the
  suspend/release plan that only ever releases what Settings itself
  suspended (refused releases stay held and are retried).
* ProfileSpaces: Private Space, Dual Apps (clone profile) and Work
  profile row states; unavailable rows explain instead of opening.

AppControlsModelTest adds 21 host tests to SettingsSableAppsModelTests.
